BT /F1 10 Tf 50 760 Td 12 TL (My own notes on onboarding corporate customers \(written for training juniors; no customer) ' (names\).) ' () ' (1. Start with the registry. Check the latest annual filing date. A filing more than 18 months) ' (old is stale: request an updated filing before going further.) ' (2. Resolve ownership layer by layer until you reach people. Anyone holding 25 percent or more,) ' (directly or through holding companies or trusts, is a beneficial owner.) ' (3. Trusts: the settlor, trustees and any protector exercise control. If the settlor also sits) ' (on the board of the customer, treat that as circular control and note it.) ' (4. Screen every director, beneficial owner, trustee and signatory against sanctions and PEP) ' (lists. A near match is cleared only on date of birth plus one other identifier, never on name) ' (alone.) ' (5. Addresses: a registered office at a virtual office provider is not on its own a reason to) ' (decline, but it raises risk when combined with layered ownership.) ' (6. Rate risk. Layered ownership through a trust plus any unresolved near match is high risk.) ' (7. The analyst recommends; an authorised approver decides. High risk always goes to the) ' (approver with the findings listed.) ' (Common junior mistakes: approving because each document looks fine on its own; missing the) ' (settlor as a beneficial owner; clearing a near match on name spelling.) ' () ' ET
endstream
